Proposed edit to https://gitlab.com/sosy-lab/sv-comp/bench-defs
File: benchmark-defs/category-structure.yml  (base: main @ 2026-09-13)

Adds SAF's 26 opt-in base categories. SAF joins NO meta category, i.e. `saf`
is deliberately absent from every `categories.<Meta>.verifiers:` list, so it is
scored only in these base categories and contributes to no Overall ranking.

Why opt_in and not opt_out: competition-scripts/test/create-benchdefs.py
purge_categories() (lines 374-397) builds the set of categories a tool runs in as
    union(leaf categories of every meta category whose verifiers/validators list
          contains the tool)
  | cs["opt_in"].get(tool_name, [])
and then deletes every <tasks> element whose name is not in that set. The word
"opt_out" never appears in create-benchdefs.py; opt_out is consumed only by
check-categories.py / the scoring scripts. For a tool in no meta category,
opt_in is therefore the ONLY thing that produces <tasks> blocks.

Verified locally (see submission/REGISTRATION.md section 6):
  * `git apply --check` against benchmark-defs/category-structure.yml @ main: OK
  * every one of the 26 entries appears in some meta category's `categories:`
    list, so check-categories.py::_check_info_consistency does not fire
    "Category used in opt_in, but missing in meta categories"
  * running the real create-benchdefs.py with this structure + the proposed
    data/saf.yml emits benchmark-defs/saf.xml with 5 rundefinitions and exactly
    26 <tasks> blocks; without this hunk it prints
    "Skipping saf for language C because: No rundefinitions left in benchmark
    definition" and writes no file at all.

Apply with:  git apply submission/category-structure.diff
(everything above the first '---' line is ignored by git apply / patch)

